A||N||3||reddog||Nitro gurus I need help!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||12-08-2001||07:18 PM||||Hey guys, I just bought a NX wet kit from 1fst2m6 along with an MSD 6A that travis put on. I am having a little trouble with a backfire in third gear though. I tried reducing the fuel jet as travis advised but I then had detonation(or backfire) in the intake. I have autolite plugs #23 gapped at 50 instead of 45. Are these plugs good or should I go with a different or colder plug? And as far as the ignition timing goes should I retard the timing a little? Also could the thermomaster chip ,power stat, and low temp coolant fan switch be farking up the performance of the MSD and nx system?  And here is a stupid question. Would rotating the distributor body without grounding the a & b terminals of the computer screw anything up? Finally could a bad map sensor connector plug cause my GT to backfire in third only when applying the spray? <BR>I love this new NX system. From first to the top of second is insane. I just would like to be able to apply the spray through all the gears though. <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||reddog||12-08-2001||09:14 PM||||bump<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||12-09-2001||05:21 PM||||Bring your plug gap down to .045 and see if that helps any.  Also when regapping your plugs check them to see if any electrodes are burnt off.  If so then back your timing off 2 degrees.  most likely what is causing the backfire is the fuel puddling in the intake system and when both valves are slightly open at the same time some of the hot gases pass back up into the intake igniting the fuel in it. Which is why I chose a dry kit cause I know that could have happened in my car and I didn't want to blow my intake through my decklid. <P>I was running stock delco plugs R42TS on my nitrous (Dry) setup for 3 years.  I burned some electrodes off but I also ran real aggressive timing and huge plug gaps as well.<P>No your temp stat and fan switch won't fark up your msd or nx system.<P>Yes a bad map sensor/connector could cause a backfire as the map can't read or send a correct signal to the computer screwing things up like spark advance.<P>So in this order do,<BR>1. retard timing<BR>2. regap plugs to .045<BR>3. check map sensor.<P>Do a drive using the nitrous after you do each of these so you can eliminate then one at a time to help diagnose it in case you have the problem again in the future.<P>keep me updated<P><P>------------------<BR>Sold Nitrous 85 GT.<BR>Looking for another.<BR>FOR SALE: Aluminum v6 block.<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
